00:12:49.940 --> 00:12:51.940
KEVIN YOUKILIS: Yes, there
are some players that

00:12:51.940 --> 00:12:54.080
are very, very into the data.

00:12:54.080 --> 00:12:56.460
There's other players
that don't want any data.

00:12:56.460 --> 00:12:59.335
There's a lot of analytics, like
driven into the pitching side

00:12:59.335 --> 00:13:00.710
because you're
really on offense.

00:13:00.710 --> 00:13:03.020
You're in control of
throwing the ball.

00:13:03.020 --> 00:13:03.710
It's like golf.

00:13:03.710 --> 00:13:05.060
The ball's sitting right there.

00:13:05.060 --> 00:13:08.120
And that's why it's become
super big, analytic-driven,

00:13:08.120 --> 00:13:11.090
because you control
what you're doing.

00:13:11.090 --> 00:13:13.670
As a hitter, you're
actually on defense.

00:13:13.670 --> 00:13:16.430
You're reacting to
what they're doing.

